WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With all the focus
on the midterms,

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.770
we haven't had enough time
to cover all the recent news,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
so here with a recap is one of
our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.076 size:75% position:38%
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.644 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:15.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys!
Things have been crazy!

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:18.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, first of all,
the President boarded a plane

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.854 line:92%
with toilet paper on his shoe.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:21.521 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I was like, "What?!"

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.758
Then he couldn't figure out
how to close his umbrella,

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he just left it
on the ground.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.695 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I was like, "What?!"

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then a dating website for
people who love Trump came out

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.534 size:78% position:39% line:92%
called Donald Daters.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:38.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that,
and I was like, "Gross."

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.572 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Then everybody was like,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Kendall Jenner culturally
appropriated an afro."

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:47.147
And I was like,
"What...are you talking about?"

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.282 size:78% position:39%
[ Australian accent ]
That's not an afro.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is an afro!

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
And then people were like,

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:55.155
"Stop talking like that,"
and I was like, "Yeah."

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, really,
that's not an afro.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a white girl who slept
at her boyfriend's house

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:03.096 line:92%
and had to use man shampoo.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.230 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Then people were mad

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
about a Martin Luther King
statue in Buffalo

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.936
because they said it looks
nothing like Martin Luther King.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"How bad could it be?"

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I saw the picture
and was like...

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.077 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[Laughing] "What?"

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
What?! That guy looks nothing
like Martin Luther King.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:23.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know who looks more like
Martin Luther King?

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This guy.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:31.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then Oprah canvassed
for Stacey Abrams in Georgia,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.692 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and I was like, "What?!"

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you imagine having Oprah
come to your door?

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
It'd be like,
"What? Is this your house?

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want my house?
I'm sorry.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.602 line:92%
I shouldn't have been in here.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:46.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on, children.
This is Oprah's house now."

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:50.376
Then at a Republican rally,
someone from Trump's cabinet

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
described Florida's
governor election as

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.117 line:92%
"cotton-pickin' important."

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.051 line:92%
I heard that and was like...

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:01.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ To tune of "Dixie" ]
Wh-wh-wh-what, wh-wh-wh-what?

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, you know
what happened today?

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.027
Idris Elba was named "People"
Magazine's Sexiest Man Alive.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:12.132
And I was like,
"Why does that sound familiar?"

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.266 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Oh, yeah. Here's why.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
Blake Shelton was named
Sexiest Man Alive,

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:21.608 size:88% position:44%
and I was like, "What...
happened to Idris Elba?

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.376 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is he okay?"

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.311 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.715 line:92%
That's right! I called it!

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:32.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm calling next year's
Sexiest Man Alive.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.053 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Idris Elba.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the year after that,
Idris Elba.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so on and so forth
until he dies,

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
at which point he will be
Sexiest Ghost Alive.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:47.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
In other news, there is a
Mandarin duck in Central Park,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.735 line:92%
and everybody is freaking out

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:52.705
because it came from China and
no one knows how it got here.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:56.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it is the most beautiful
bird I have ever seen.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:03:00.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that Chinese duck,
and I was like...

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.917 size:81% position:41%
Back here in America,
white ladies have been

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:09.055
calling the cops on black people
for the stupidest reasons.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.957 line:92%
She called 911 on a black man

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was planting
a community garden.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
She called the cops
on a black guy

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was entering
his own apartment.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she called him
on a 9-year-old child

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.500 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for just living.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.334 line:92%
I read all that and was like

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:24.871
"Well, surely, this can't
get any more ridiculous."

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.406 line:92%
And that's when it happened.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:31.611
White people who were on a boat
called the police on a whale!

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Look!

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:36.816 size:81% position:41%
-It's fine. It's fine.
It's right under us.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.351 line:92%
-Um, I'm out in Puget Sound,

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.821
and there's three whales
right underneath our boat,

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm afraid that
we might get flipped over.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Drive away.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I saw that
and was like, "What?"

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:57.136
You can't call the cops on a
whale when you're in the ocean.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.705 size:75% position:38% line:92%
You're in his house.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
He should call the police
on you.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:02.175 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Now, don't get me wrong.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.978
If you come downstairs and
see a whale out your window,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.312 size:84% position:42% line:92%
please call the police.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:11.184
And finally, it is the end
of a very long Election Day.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:14.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, to Democrats,
I just want to say,

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:15.521 size:75% position:38% line:92%
you campaigned hard,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
you registered
thousands of new voters,

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you had a lot
of firsts tonight.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:23.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
First openly gay male governor
in history. What?!

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.131 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:28.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
Massachusetts' first black
Congresswoman. What?!

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.169 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
Connecticut's first black
Congresswoman. What?!

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
The youngest
Congresswoman ever! What?!

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:42.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
Texas' first two Latina
Congresswomen. What, what?!

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.616 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And the first two Muslim

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:46.786 size:88% position:44%
and the first two Native
American Congresswomen.

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:49.155 size:88% position:44% line:92%
What, what, what, what?!

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.090 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah!

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:55.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to Republicans,
I just want to say, "What?"

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:58.665 line:92%
This has been "Amber Says What."

